#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f6f3cc2-e0b5-5263-896d-53369438a2f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Midpoint Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "f46e0c53-c110-5990-b3ea-5dd27991cdc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2557" :question/problem "Which number corresponds to the midpoint of the line segment $\\overline{AB}$ shown below?\n\n![](images/88/8850f207b51c6789073a0fb83b221a93290ade40b3f148248cac803fc1486452.png)" :question/worked-solution "The point $A$ corresponds to the number $x_1=-1$ while $B$ corresponds to $x_2=5.$ \n\nTo find the number $x_m$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midpoint $M$ corresponds to $x_m=2.$\n\n![](images/07/07d9c940fbe2e5a14c5dc3fc1b46add8947f9ad0df7151f8693793cf70359688.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110378 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb88880e-8b94-5223-b3fb-a4d80e795a00" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Midpoints to Calculate an Unknown Value From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "7c337d65-54d7-5264-b750-1a7f7bcd07f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-2558" :question/problem "Given that $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{PQ}$, what is the value of $x?$\n\n![](images/bf/bf08731ef8b88b55c1b3df41e58443beefb5e1a69b46757fbfb18c22d6c0b6b1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{PQ}$, the segment $\\overline{PQ}$ is twice the length of the segment $\\overline{PM}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2PM & =PQ \\\\ 2(4x-3) & =5x+9 \\\\ 8x-6 & =5x+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we subtract $5x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-6-5x & =5x+9-5x \\\\ 3x-6 & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $6$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-6+6 & =9+6 \\\\ 3x & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by $3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110379 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4a4cad5-d0b0-51cb-921f-31a96e8e5eda" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Midpoints to Calculate an Unknown Value From a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "6e321a78-087f-5962-a88c-e61bdc10de9f" :question/math-academy-id "e-2559" :question/problem "The point $M$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overline{LN}.$ What is the value of $x$ if $MN=4x+1$ centimeters and $LM=3x+4$ centimeters?" :question/worked-solution "We have the following diagram.\n\n![](images/60/60e50f27aef61d5a97f9165dab922fa25cd80c114a0b11bbfbcdfe4c0fdf90e9.png)\n\nSince $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{LN}$, the two segments $\\overline{LM}$ and $\\overline{MN}$ have the same length. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LM & =MN \\\\ 3x+4 & =4x+1 \\\\ 3x+4-3x & =4x+1-3x \\\\ 4 & =x+1 \\\\ 4-1 & =x+1-1 \\\\ 3 & =x \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x = 3\\,\\textrm{cm}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c451d750-c40f-5b3f-9cd2-9eec197809de" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Midpoint Formula to Calculate an Endpoint"}] :question/id #uuid "c79d8054-b4f5-57e3-b816-5ac07ccfa90d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2560" :question/problem "For the diagram depicted below, which number corresponds to the point $R$ if $M$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overline{RS}?$\n\n![](images/d4/d4b49c7832633378a281295850be72f2ff664475b79f9b692591411c2d9ed6c4.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we can see that the point $S$ corresponds to the number $x_2=3$ while the midpoint $M$ corresponds to $x_m=1.$ \n\nTo find the number $x_1$ corresponding to the point $R$, we first set up an equation using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $x_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+3}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & ={x}_{1}+3 \\\\ 2 & ={x}_{1}+3 \\\\ 2-3 & ={x}_{1} \\\\ -1 & ={x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $R$ corresponds to $x_1=-1.$\n\n![](images/f4/f4897cf174e575e4999ba9605c9ddd03b3820c63fd77a1d7f87fdcaac171e35b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4a4cad5-d0b0-51cb-921f-31a96e8e5eda" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Midpoints to Calculate an Unknown Value From a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f6b112a-d93c-5fc6-a73a-27598047dc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492245} {:answer/id #uuid "236db9c2-e961-5bb6-885a-1f1d59ebc53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492291} {:answer/id #uuid "458cd1a3-a1aa-5855-b581-1927993cc51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492354} {:answer/id #uuid "b458f1a4-6de9-5ebc-8ac6-549866246f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492579} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c6b138-e3ec-5ccd-9fd8-67386d49d803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b458f1a4-6de9-5ebc-8ac6-549866246f27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492579} :answer-field/id #uuid "f14532b2-89c3-5054-aee7-a57741f4303d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0be3393b-3971-5aa6-969d-c38ead885b36" :question/math-academy-id "q-113576" :question/problem "The point $S$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}.$ What is the value of $x$ if $SQ=x+9$ inches and $PS=2x+5$ inches?" :question/worked-solution "We have the following diagram.\n\n![](images/29/29610a9e6bc2d25522c151c1676d438a860503e640bf9f7beb178ab73b3b6be7.png)\n\nSince $S$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$, the two segments $\\overset{―}{PS}$ and $\\overset{―}{SQ}$ have the same length. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PS & =SQ \\\\ 2x+5 & =x+9 \\\\ 2x+5-x & =x+9-x \\\\ x+5 & =9 \\\\ x+5-5 & =9-5 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=4\\,\\text{in}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f6f3cc2-e0b5-5263-896d-53369438a2f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Midpoint Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "650c8bff-e687-5da4-a1f8-c7555e64334e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492419} {:answer/id #uuid "6f1f643c-b8fc-56a9-8dd4-06ca17aab578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492437} {:answer/id #uuid "c7635f8a-eb66-5317-a9c4-ce65c5eed39d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492615} {:answer/id #uuid "d258c475-bcf1-5ae5-af36-ca166b557172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb