int $A$ corresponds to the number ${x}_{1}=-4$ while $B$ corresponds to ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ea/eaf87888628f29d0025632a98df3d778307b1cfdb4538d997529db13c8518aba.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb88880e-8b94-5223-b3fb-a4d80e795a00" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Midpoints to Calculate an Unknown Value From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e13d289-40f7-54a4-9717-d352aeee2b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492239} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfac727-e2fc-5c11-9d30-76d859133d1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492277} {:answer/id #uuid "5afea3dd-7207-5156-ba7f-4d58e8541903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492396} {:answer/id #uuid "6295bc07-b016-5675-9854-4c43d931438d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492417} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ac2b40-816a-5a08-bf36-e6f8fea98296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afea3dd-7207-5156-ba7f-4d58e8541903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492396} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d2837ff-017e-5662-9265-9dc9e2a07f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20dca1bf-125b-5100-89df-0e22487e711f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71742" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a38ed00f3b3ac3741c7766f6b344dae59ba6e538e0fb210382bab7f0377eb0d0.png)\n\nGiven that $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is twice the length of the segment $\\overset{―}{AM}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2AM & =AB \\\\ 2(3x-2) & =4x+6 \\\\ 6x-4 & =4x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we subtract $4x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-4-4x & =4x+6-4x \\\\ 2x-4 & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-4+4 & =6+4 \\\\ 2x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
